|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y1NWXC53CjM|year=2020|time=16:26|text=The '''fourth estate''' is a term to describe the power that journalists and news media have to keep the powers of government in check by informing the citizens. The way citizens have received news and information has always evolved, but throughout that whole time, having an informed audience was seen as a necessity to a functioning democracy. The newspaper itself has been dying for a while, even before social media, all thanks to 24-hour news.}}

